MJnethack@gmail.com wrote:
>I just totally screwed up my most promising game ever putting a wand
>of cancellation into my bag of holding.  I had been careful several
>times before, but this time I overlooked it.  Apparently from reading
>spoilers even putting them in a sack is not a safe way to keep
>yourself from these sort of accidents.  What tricks have you all come
>up with to keep yourself from doing this dumb thing?

Engrave-id each new type of wand as soon as I find it; if it's not
obvious, #name "quiet" or "vanish" appropriately, and be paranoid about
stashing "vanish".

Never, ever use "," when putting items into a bag and the visible set
includes wands. Train yourself to be almost superstitiously afraid of
this. I don't put wands of cancellation in sacks these days because I
find it too hard to remember that the sack is also dangerous, although I
guess better #naming habits would help.

As soon as I find cancellation, BURY IT UNDER A GREAT BIG BOULDER.

Before starting the ascension run, prepare an emergency stash somewhere
up near DL1 with whatever you can spare of holy water, remove curse,
gold detection, wands of teleportation, wands of death, and the like,
and ideally a spare bag of holding. Make sure to carry at least one of
each of teleportation and death in your main inventory. If you blow up
your bag before the ascension run, you'll have time to refill it, but if
you've already killed the Wizard then you won't have time. Don't carry
the stuff you need for the Planes while going down for the Amulet; stash
it instead and pick it up on the way.

In general, don't carry everything with you. You aren't likely to need
more than (say) 10 potions of holy water even on a dive into Gehennom.
Stash your stuff so that it's not so vulnerable to a single accident.

Try not to get into a situation where you have a cursed bag of holding
in the first place. As long as you aren't excessively burdened with it
blessed, if it becomes uncursed, you ought to still be able to #dip it
almost immediately. Don't leave it at the uncursed stage unless you
absolutely have to. If you're worried about multiple curses while
fighting a single nasty monster, a useful strategy is sometimes to carry
a bunch of worthless light items (like gems) in your main inventory,
#named to keep them separate, to reduce the probability that your bag
takes the curse.


My first ascension featured an incident where I put a sack containing
two wands of cancellation into a bag of holding (I was actually trying
to look inside the sack) just before starting the ascension run.
Fortunately I had just prepared a stash for the Planes as above on DL1,
and I could go back up and fetch enough to get by, even though I did
have to be more careful than before.

